    "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::test-singleton-env-var-coupling": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::test-singleton-env-var-coupling",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "Test DB/Redis singletons silently skip when env vars are unset, hiding missing-dependency failures",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "initialization_coupling",
        "related_files": [
          "test/testutil/db.go",
          "test/testutil/testutil.go"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "test/testutil/db.go:29-31 returns t.Skip() when TEST_DATABASE_URL is empty; test/testutil/testutil.go:123-125 returns nil when TEST_REDIS_URL is empty. The sync.Once means the first test that runs without the env var permanently sets the nil/error state for the entire process. A subsequent test run with the env var set (e.g., via os.Setenv in a different test) would still get nil because the Once already fired."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Document the singleton behavior prominently or consider per-test connections instead of process-level singletons. At minimum, add a comment at the var declarations warning that the Once fires on first call regardless of env var presence.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "442e3299"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
      "first_seen": "2026-05-08T11:00:09+00:00",
